MODIFICATIONS
-------------

In accordance with section 5(a) of the GNU General Public License v3.0, this
file records that Subbox is a modified version of Feishin, and the nature and
dates of those modifications.

Modified by Luke Purnell, from 2024 onwards. The principal changes are:

  * Renamed the application from "Feishin" to "Subbox", with new branding,
    icons, and landing page.

  * Added integration with the pymix API — a separate backend service, not
    part of this program — for converting music libraries and playlists
    between DJ software (Rekordbox, Serato) and Subsonic/Navidrome.

  * Added the Sync feature area: library upload, watch-directory uploading,
    playlist download, and Rekordbox/Serato import and export.

  * Added a wishlist feature (item management, link parsing, and reconciliation
    against the user's library).

  * Added track and playlist sharing surfaces.

  * Added a file-browser integration and per-user container awareness for
    Subbox's hosted deployment model.

  * Added a demo-account mode that restricts write operations in the UI.

  * Numerous consequential changes to routing, state stores, settings, and
    build configuration to support the above.

The complete, authoritative record of every modification is the git history of
the Subbox repository:

    https://github.com/laker-93/subbox-app

Unmodified upstream Feishin code retains the copyright of its original authors.


